Command scripts for building Yale Haskell under SBCL (tested with
SBCL 2.6 on arm64 macOS).  They are POSIX sh, and need only SBCL on
the PATH (or $SBCL set).  Y2 defaults to the root of the checkout.

  com/sbcl/compile        compile the Lisp sources of the compiler
  com/sbcl/build-prelude  compile the standard prelude
  com/sbcl/savesys        save bin/sbcl-haskell.core
  com/sbcl/clean          delete all SBCL binaries

Compiled files go in an "sbcl" subdirectory of each source directory.

To run:

  bin/yale-haskell             interactive command interface
  bin/yale-haskell foo.hs      compile foo.hs and run Main.main
